Notes before you send:

1. **The function does not remove opted-out people.** It only sets `opted_out` to "Y" or "N". Filter on `opted_out == "N"` before the send list is built.

2. **Opt-outs can be lost in step 9.** Rows with no valid email or phone are dropped before matching, so an opt-out row with bad contact details can't match and suppress the same person's valid row. For example, if one row has a good email and another row with the same name has an opt-out and a malformed email, the person still gets emailed. Before sending, check the final list against a separate suppression list built from every opted-out row in the raw export, matching on any valid email or phone. Your data person or legal should confirm this, since opt-out honoring matters for this campaign.

